================================================================================
Engine binary dependencies
================================================================================

The cairn engine is a Rust binary. Every crate it links (including the
tree-sitter grammars and the bundled SQLite and sqlite-vec builds) is declared
in Cargo.lock; their licenses are checked on every change by cargo-deny
against the allow-list in rust/deny.toml (Apache-2.0, Apache-2.0 WITH
LLVM-exception, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, CC0-1.0, ISC, MIT, Unicode-3.0,
Zlib). The lockfile is the authoritative inventory; `cargo deny list` in
rust/ renders it.

================================================================================
PyPI package
================================================================================

The `cairn-intel` wheel is the engine binary (a maturin bin wheel): it
contains no Python code and declares no runtime dependencies.

================================================================================
Vendored content (dashboard static assets)
================================================================================

The dashboard vendors the minified standalone browser builds of the
third-party libraries below as static assets. They are carried in-tree under
rust/crates/cairn-cli/dashboard-assets/static/, embedded into the cairn binary
(rust/crates/cairn-cli/src/dashboard/assets.rs) and served by its dashboard;
no bundler or CDN is used at runtime.

